# Supabase SQL Source of Truth

When changing the Supabase/Postgres database, update the greenfield deploy scripts in the same change (same PR/commit as the `af_*.sql` edit). Deploy live DB changes via the Supabase MCP tools (`apply_migration` / `execute_sql`) — do **not** create one-off `sql/migration_*.sql` files.

## Schema (tables, columns, indexes, RLS, seed data)

- **Canonical file:** `sql/supabase_schema_create.sql`
- **Required:** put new columns/constraints in the relevant `CREATE TABLE` (or equivalent) in `supabase_schema_create.sql`
- **Deploy:** apply the schema change to the live DB via MCP; do not add a `migration_*.sql` file

## Functions (RPCs, triggers implemented as functions)

- **Canonical file:** `sql/supabase_functions_create.sql`
- **Also add/update:** the matching `sql/af_*.sql` (or other function file) for the single-function source path
- **Required:** copy the full updated `CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION` (and `DROP`/`GRANT` signature changes) into `supabase_functions_create.sql` so running that script deploys the latest functions
- **Deploy:** apply the function to the live DB via MCP; do not add a `migration_*.sql` file

## Checklist before finishing SQL work

1. Live DB updated via Supabase MCP (no `sql/migration_*.sql` file)
2. `supabase_schema_create.sql` reflects any new schema
3. Matching `sql/af_*.sql` exists/updated for function changes
4. `supabase_functions_create.sql` reflects any changed function bodies or signatures
5. Old function signatures are dropped where signatures changed (see top-of-file `DROP FUNCTION` block in `supabase_functions_create.sql` when applicable)

Do not treat individual `af_*.sql` files alone as sufficient for a fresh database or full function redeploy — keep `supabase_functions_create.sql` (and schema create) in sync.
